{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205497-just-hatched-dragon-blooded","id":1205497,"title":"Just Hatched Dragon-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T01:27:20-07:00","id":1205497,"title":"Just Hatched Dragon-Blooded","content":"Anyone else find these rules make newly Exalted Dragon-Blooded beefier than expected? It's roughly the same gap as between Essence 1 and 2 Solars, but those rules are assuming adult-to-more-experienced-adult progression. I'd have thought newly Exalted DBs, being 14 or so, would have a bigger gap from their Essence 2 adult selves. It doesn't come off for example that a lot of actual abilities get developed at the Dynasty's Secondary Schools (though I realize that the problem there is you don't want to penalize outcaste Dragon-Blooded with fewer Ability dots or Charms on top of their fewer merits dots).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of trying to make the &quot;just hatched&quot; come of more as undeveloped kids relative to adult DBs...<br /> <br /> Something like 6/4/3 Attribute spread, 20 ability dots, 7 Charms, 7 Merit dots (regardless of background, the bonus for Dynasts and equivalents comes after graduation), Essence 1, and 15 bonus points.<br /> <br /> Make the Essence 2 upgrade come after 200 xp or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-11-2018, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:13:13-07:00","id":1205559,"title":"","content":"Yeah but I figured it was handwavium, like allowing an Exaltation in play result in knowing all your charms by the first downtime. I'd probably build them a bit less, and hand out free upgrades throughout the game/school seasons. Like when Exalting I don't hand out all the charms, usually about 4 or so and distribute the rest of the 15 over the first year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T11:03:14-07:00","id":1205680,"title":"","content":"If I were to run a Secondary School game myself, I don\u2019t think i\u2019d bother with xp. If the characters were starting as first years, I\u2019d have them build their characters as I described in my first post, and then hand out Charms, attribute dots, etc as they aged and trained, until they matched a starting Essence 2 Dragon Blooded at graduation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:41:05-07:00","id":1205821,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Struck me that two different tiers may be helpful, both for brand newly Exalted tweens, and for older teens half way through their education.<br /> <br /> For Essence 1, recently Exalted young adolescents</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Attributes are 6/4/3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 15 Ability dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 2 Specialties</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 5 Merit dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 4 Charms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 10 bonus points</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">For older adolescents who have already been Exalted for years, but are still well off from graduation (if Realm)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Attributes 7/5/3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 20 Ability dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 4 Specialties (1 of which should reflect your school/background)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 7 Merit dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 10 Charms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- 15 bonus points</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Essence 2, but no Charms at Essence 2 unless bought with bonus points</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T02:31:26-07:00","id":1205971,"title":"","content":"I'd probably give tweens 5 charms, just because it feels weird if it's not a multiple of 5. <br /> <br /> I do like the &quot;essence 2, but no essence 2 charms without bonus points&quot;. That's quite clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}